{"id": "EUVD-2026-107240", "enisaUuid": "86a0fa87-7b27-32e2-b018-578668dc6bfe", "description": "Trudesk through 1.2.11 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows any authenticated user to modify tickets outside their groups via PUT /api/v1/tickets/:id and PUT /api/v2/tickets/batch. Attackers can supply arbitrary ticket ObjectIds to change status, subject, group, priority or assignee, or mass-close tickets, since only the default tickets:update role grant is checked.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T12:39:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:48", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/multiple-vuln-trudesk-1211", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk/blob/v1.2.11/src/controllers/api/v1/tickets.js#L767-L883", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk/blob/v1.2.11/src/controllers/api/v2/tickets.js#L167-L197", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/trudesk-through-1.2.11-authorization-bypass-via-ticket-update-api-endpoints"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114393", "GHSA-hqv6-jg73-3gmv"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "333281aa-4132-3658-85f8-d955d6a3a676", "product": {"name": "trudesk", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d160667b-ea33-3604-8184-57741ecefde6", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}], "isExploited": false}